\begin{align*}
d &= \sqrt{(0-3)^2+(1-(-5))^2+(1-7)^2}\\
&=\sqrt{9+36+36}\\
&= \sqrt{81}\\
&= 9
\end{align*}
Let $r$ be the radius of the circle of intersection. Using the RMR formula for two intersecting spheres, we have:
\begin{align*}
r^2&=r_1^2+d^2-r_2^2\\
&=50+81-68\\
&=63
\end{align*}
